    "interconnection": "The Sorcerer first freezes a connected lower bridge and its tall spillway. That bridge carries the knight to his first ward. A far sluice thaws and drains the same bridge: the spillway no longer stops the next cast. A redirected cast then freezes his upper ward into the return landing, reached with the original anvil. The final route returns above the drained crossing through mirrored glass.",
    "solution": "Wait for his first cast to freeze the lower bridge, cross it, and wound him on the ice. Continue to the far sluice and cut its visible brass wheel. The lower bridge drains, including the tall spillway that blocked his next cast. From the anvil alcove, parry Up-Right into the upper pool. Pogo the anvil, dash through the mirror boundary, and cut his exposed upper ward. Use the frozen upper landing to cross the mirror back and return along the high islands to the gate above your original fire.",
    "novelty": "The same frozen water first supports travel and then obstructs the next returning projectile; removing it opens the boss interaction but erases the old foot route. The upper ward is also the permanent return landing after the actual boss defeat.",
    "nearestExisting": "F18 water/weight state and F49 removal of the outward route become one native Sorcerer fight with mirrored return.",
